"text": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv) and (d)-(v)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258abd"}, {"id": "5f1ea7", "text": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(v) and (d)-(iv)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258abe"}, {"id": "01b480", "text": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii) and (d)-(v)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258abf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ac0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b64"], "question": {"text": "Among the following, the molecule expected to be stabilized by anion formation is:<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "42856a", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ac1"}, {"id": "b27061", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ac2"}, {"id": "fd47de", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ac3"}, {"id": "3bdada", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ac4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ac5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["617aa9e9ef3fe65ad8e837f2"], "question": {"text": "The correct statement/s about Hydrogen bonding is/are\nA. Hydrogen bonding exists when \\(\\mathrm{H}\\) is covalently bonded to the highly electro negative atom.\nB. Intermolecular \\(\\mathrm{H}\\) bonding is present in o-nitro phenol\nC. Intramolecular \\(\\mathrm{H}\\) bonding is present in HF.\nD. The magnitude of \\(\\mathrm{H}\\) bonding depends on the physical state of the compound.\nE. H-bonding has powerful effect on the structure and properties of compounds\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "021983", "text": "A, B, D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ac6"}, {"id": "da3113", "text": "A, D, E only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ac7"}, {"id": "6b6c6e", "text": "A only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ac8"}, {"id": "7446e4", "text": "A, B, C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ac9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258aca", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f44"], "concepts": ["6162fb836ed13040ec84fc98"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p>Statement I:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SbCl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> is more covalent than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SbCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Statement II: The higher oxides of halogens also tend to be more stable than the lower ones.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "0c4d57", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but statement II is correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258acb"}, {"id": "dedcc0", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258acc"}, {"id": "680ea3", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258acd"}, {"id": "c9eb93", "text": "Statement I is correct but statement II is incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ace"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258acf", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4771"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87e0"], "question": {"text": "<p>The increasing order of boiling points of the following compounds is :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fd6f48716-1af5-4252-b658-b112767bb3f1-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 303px; height: 192px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9e3a4c", "text": "I &lt; III &lt; IV &lt; II", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ad0"}, {"id": "872542", "text": "I &lt; IV &lt; II&lt; III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ad1"}, {"id": "22c3d0", "text": "IV &lt; I &lt; II &lt; III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ad2"}, {"id": "131f93", "text": "III &lt; I &lt; II &lt; IV", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ad3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ad4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e567ac499d1e49588f95f5"], "concepts": ["6210dfdd59c631201791bc49"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements : One is labelled as Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and the other is labelled as Reason&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math></p><p>Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> : Zero orbital overlap is an out of phase overlap.</p><p>Reason&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> : It results due to different orientation/ direction of approach of orbitals.</p><p>In the light of the above statements. Choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d1a260", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;are true and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;is the correct explanation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ad5"}, {"id": "738469", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> are true but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is NOT the correct explanation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ad6"}, {"id": "5dd130", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is true but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ad7"}, {"id": "23bc26", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is false but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ad8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ad9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b3f"], "question": {"text": "The molecules having square pyramidal geometry are"}, "options": [{"id": "338c1c", "text": "$\\mathrm{BrF}_5 \\& \\mathrm{PCl}_5$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ada"}, {"id": "8bdf45", "text": "$\\mathrm{SbF}_5 \\& \\mathrm{PCl}_5$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258adb"}, {"id": "376a93", "text": "$\\mathrm{SbF}_5 \\& \\mathrm{XeOF}_4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258adc"}, {"id": "edaeb3", "text": "$\\mathrm{BrF}_5 \\& \\mathrm{XeOF}_4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258add"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ade", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52be"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following molecules(s) show/s paramagnetic behavior?<br />(A) $\\mathrm{O}_2$<br />(B) $\\mathrm{N}_2$<br />(C) $\\mathrm{F}_2$<br />(D) $\\mathrm{S}_2$<br />(E) $\\mathrm{Cl}_2$<br />Choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "21972b", "text": "B only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258adf"}, {"id": "041d49", "text": "A & C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ae0"}, {"id": "ed584b", "text": "A & E only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ae1"}, {"id": "b0faad", "text": "A & D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ae2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ae3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4771"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4727"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements : one is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R).\nAssertion (A) : \\(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\) and \\(\\mathrm{NF}_3\\) molecule have pyramidal shape with a lone pair of electrons on nitrogen atom. The resultant dipole moment of \\(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\) is greater than that of \\(\\mathrm{NF}_3\\).\nReason (R) : In \\(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\), the orbital dipole due to lone pair is in the same direction as the resultant dipole moment of the \\(\\mathrm{N}-\\mathrm{H}\\) bonds. \\(\\mathrm{F}\\) is the most electronegative element.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "1e2c5b", "text": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ae4"}, {"id": "5065f8", "text": "(A) is false but (R) is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ae5"}, {"id": "7dac2e", "text": "Both (A) and (R) are true but \\((\\mathbf{R})\\) is NOT the correct explanation of (A)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ae6"}, {"id": "e116fb", "text": "(A) is true but \\((\\mathbf{R})\\) is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ae7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ae8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["61ab79db6fe44bfe0fe4b3bb"], "question": {"text": "<p>Consider the following molecules and statements related to them:</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fbfa61275-504f-4409-97c9-4a19621b8051-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 472px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>(a) (B) is more likely to be crystaline than (A)</p><p>(b) (B) has higher boiling point than (A)</p><p>(c) (B) dissolves more readily than (A) in water</p><p>Identify the correct option from below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "92ad00", "text": "(a) and (b) are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258ae9"}, {"id": "cf5efa", "text": "(a) and (c) are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258aea"}, {"id": "b88151", "text": "only (a) is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258aeb"}, {"id": "3f3f8d", "text": "(b) and (c) are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258aec"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258aed", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f44"], "concepts": ["6162fb836ed13040ec84fc98"], "question": {"text": "The correct set from the following in which both pairs are in correct order of melting point is:"}, "options": [{"id": "f012d5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiF</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>LiCl</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>NaCl</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>MgO</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258aee"}, {"id": "c1dbd2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiCl</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>LiF</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>MgO</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>NaCl</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258aef"}, {"id": "a1a691", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiCl</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>LiF</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>NaCl</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>MgO</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258af0"}, {"id": "36ff07", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiF</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>LiCl</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>MgO</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>NaCl</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258af1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258af2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["6117b89067dbe2603c3e80ce"], "question": {"text": "Number of lone pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math> of electrons on central atom and the shape of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> molecule respectively, are :<br />&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "38e67e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math> , triangular planar.<br />&nbsp;", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258af3"}, {"id": "fd7eb8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> , pyramidal.<br />&nbsp;", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258af4"}, {"id": "dea97b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> , bent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>-shape.<br />&nbsp;", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258af5"}, {"id": "3b257e", "text": "&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>, bent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>-shape", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258af6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258af7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa028"], "question": {"text": "The bond dissociation energy is highest for"}, "options": [{"id": "ed9f58", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258af8"}, {"id": "9bd5d9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258af9"}, {"id": "6a1bdd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258afa"}, {"id": "78c33e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258afb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258afc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95d3"], "question": {"text": "<p>Match the type of interaction in column <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> with the distance dependence of their interaction energy in column <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>:</mo></math></p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 300px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>A</strong></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>B</strong></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(i)&nbsp;ion -&nbsp;ion&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>(a)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(ii) Dipole - dipole</td>\t\t\t<td>(b)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(iii) London dispersion</td>\t\t\t<td>(c)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>(iv)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>"}, "options": [{"id": "d46dea", "text": "&nbsp;(i) &ndash; (b); (ii) &ndash; (d); (iii) &ndash; (c)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258afd"}, {"id": "8ebeef", "text": "&nbsp;(i) &ndash; (a); (ii) &ndash; (b); (iii) &ndash; (d)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258afe"}, {"id": "a7baf6", "text": "(i) &ndash; (a); (ii) &ndash; (b); (iii) &ndash; (c)&nbsp;", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258aff"}, {"id": "ed2a47", "text": "(i) &ndash; (a); (ii) &ndash; (c); (iii) &ndash; (d)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b00"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b01", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4771"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4727"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements:<br/>Statement-I: Since fluorine is more electronegative than nitrogen, the net dipole moment of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.<br/>Statement-II: In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>, the orbital dipole due to lone pair and the dipole moment of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NH</mi></math> bonds are in opposite direction, but in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> the orbital dipole due to lone pair and dipole moments of N-F bonds are in same direction.<br/>In the light of the above statements. Choose the most appropriate from the options given below."}, "options": [{"id": "c9f1e3", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b02"}, {"id": "dfea18", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b03"}, {"id": "c19393", "text": "Both statement I and Statement II is are true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b04"}, {"id": "3265b6", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is are true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b05"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b06", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f44"], "concepts": ["6162fb836ed13040ec84fc98"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements: One is labelled as Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and the other labelled as Reason <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> : Lithium halides are some what covalent in nature.</p><p>Reason <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> : Lithium possess high polarisation capability.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e67547", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is true but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b07"}, {"id": "417a2c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is false but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b08"}, {"id": "ed1933", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> are true but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is NOT the correct explanation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b09"}, {"id": "baf7a1", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> are true and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is the correct explanation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b0a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b0b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9947"], "question": {"text": "<p>Among the following molecules/ ions,&nbsp;</p><p><math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math></p><p>Which one is diamagnetic and has the shortest bond length?</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d19e22", "text": "<math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b0c"}, {"id": "fcd366", "text": "<math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b0d"}, {"id": "dbae14", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b0e"}, {"id": "b71f94", "text": "<math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b0f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b10", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["6162fb816ed13040ec84fae9"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following statement is true with respect to $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}, \\mathrm{NH}_3$ and $\\mathrm{CH}_4$ ?\nA. The central atoms of all the molecules are $\\mathrm{sp}^3$ hybridized.\nB. The $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{O}-\\mathrm{H}, \\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{N}-\\mathrm{H}$ and $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ angles in the above molecules are $104.5^{\\circ}, 107.5^{\\circ}$ and $109.5^{\\circ}$, respectively.\nC. The increasing order of dipole moment is $\\mathrm{CH}_4 \\lt \\mathrm{NH}_3 \\lt \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}$.\nD. Both $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}$ and $\\mathrm{NH}_3$ are Lewis acids and $\\mathrm{CH}_4$ is a Lewis base.\nE. A solution of $\\mathrm{NH}_3$ in $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}$ is basic. In this solution $\\mathrm{NH}_3$ and $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}$ act as Lowry-Bronsted acid and base respectively.\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "fd2018", "text": "A, B and C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b11"}, {"id": "f6df45", "text": "A, D and E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b12"}, {"id": "3b417e", "text": "C, D and E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b13"}, {"id": "064160", "text": "A, B, C and E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b14"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b15", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["6117b94a67dbe2603c3e9983"], "question": {"text": "<p>The compound/s which will show significant intermolecular <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-bonding is/are :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fff944fa7-b3a1-4c48-96d9-181fe7420bed-8e72dbfd-89af-4744-9f67-8afb69fdc282-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 470px; height: 137px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "df3549", "text": "(a), (b) and (c)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b16"}, {"id": "e5351b", "text": "(b) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b17"}, {"id": "eeab3b", "text": "(c) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b18"}, {"id": "781f9b", "text": "(a) and (b) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b19"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b1a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4771"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87e0"], "question": {"text": "<p>Among the following compounds, the one which shows highest dipole moment is</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "cb02af", "text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fda9d7330-6f8d-4f1e-b02b-d014775bde4d.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 100px; height: 113px;\" /></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b1b"}, {"id": "4e9058", "text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F58dfd10c-38b4-48d1-83ec-98cce7bb0f58.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 98px;\" /></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b1c"}, {"id": "e771bc", "text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fd27a6b50-db37-4a5b-8138-53e6653bc45a.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 91px;\" /></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3e2ee0e063d9258b1d"}, {"id": "f68f45", "text": "<p>